# 🧑‍💼 Gestion Équipe — Astreinte + Daily Tasks

## The Two Operational Layers

Your team runs on **two distinct but linked concepts**:

```
LAYER 1 — Weekly Astreinte (Rotation)
─────────────────────────────────────
  Week 1: Mohammed 📞  ← Any incident? He picks up.
  Week 2: Yasser   📞
  Week 3: Hamza    📞
  ...
  Automatic rotation, everyone knows who's on duty.

LAYER 2 — Daily Task Assignments (Manager assigns)
───────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Monday 21/04:
    Yasser  → Reprise d'incident (if declared)
    Hamza   → MEP in production at 07:00
    Rachid  → Create the daily board / tableau de bord
    Amine   → Night: Supervise la chaîne compta

  Weekend 26-27/04:
    Ahmed   → Supervise incidents all weekend
```

These two layers work together: the **astreinte person** is the 24/7 fallback;
the **daily tasks** are the planned operational duties for that specific day.

---

## 📅 Layer 1 — Astreinte Rotation

### What it means
- One person per week is **"de astreinte"** (on-call)
- If **any incident is declared** → they are the primary responder
- This rotates weekly across team members (e.g. round-robin)
- Everyone can see **who is on astreinte this week** at a glance

### UI — Astreinte Widget (visible on Dashboard)

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  📞 Astreinte — Semaine 17 (21-27 Avr)          │
│  ─────────────────────────────────────────────  │
│  👤 Mohammed Alami       📱 +212 6XX XXX XXX    │
│     Équipe Production    Fin: Dimanche 23:59     │
│  ─────────────────────────────────────────────  │
│  Semaine prochaine → Yasser Benali              │
│  [Voir planning complet]                         │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Data Model

```prisma
/// Weekly on-call rotation — one person per team per week
model Astreinte {
  id          String   @id @default(uuid())
  weekNumber  Int                             // ISO week number (1-52)
  year        Int
  startDate   DateTime                        // Monday 00:00
  endDate     DateTime                        // Sunday 23:59

  teamId      String
  team        Team     @relation(fields: [teamId], references: [id])

  userId      String                          // who is on astreinte
  user        User     @relation("AstreinteUser", fields: [userId], references: [id])

  phone       String?                         // direct phone for this week
  notes       String?                         // any special instructions

  createdById String
  createdBy   User     @relation("AstreinteCreatedBy", fields: [createdById], references: [id])

  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt   DateTime @updatedAt

  @@unique([teamId, weekNumber, year])        // one person per team per week
  @@index([teamId])
  @@index([userId])
  @@index([startDate, endDate])
}
```

### Endpoints

| Method | Path | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| `GET` | `/api/v1/astreintes` | List astreintes (filter by team, year) |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/astreintes/current` | Who is on duty **right now** |
| `POST` | `/api/v1/astreintes` | Assign astreinte for a week |
| `PATCH` | `/api/v1/astreintes/:id` | Change the person (replacement) |
| `DELETE` | `/api/v1/astreintes/:id` | Remove |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/astreintes/planning` | Full yearly rotation calendar |

---

## 📋 Layer 2 — Daily Operational Tasks

### What it means
The manager opens the app and assigns tasks to each team member for a **specific day**
(or weekend). Each task has a **type/role**, a **time slot**, and a **target** (system, chain, etc.).

### Real examples from your team

| Who | Task | Time | System/Domain |
|-----|------|------|---------------|
| Yasser | Reprise d'incident (si déclarée) | Morning | Any system |
| Hamza | MEP en production | 07:00 | Target system |
| Rachid | Créer tableau de bord du jour | Start of day | — |
| Amine | Superviser la chaîne compta | Night | Chaîne compta |
| Ahmed | Supervision incidents (weekend) | All day | All systems |

### Task Types (Enum)

```prisma
enum OperationalTaskType {
  ASTREINTE_BACKUP    // Backup responder for incidents
  MEP                 // Mise En Production (deployment)
  SUPERVISION         // Supervise a system or chain
  TABLEAU_BORD        // Create/maintain daily dashboard/board
  REPRISE_INCIDENT    // Take over ongoing incident recovery
  CONTROLE_CHAINE     // Control/verify a processing chain
  RAPPORT             // Write a report
  CUSTOM              // Free text task
}
```

### Data Model

```prisma
/// A day's operational task plan — groups tasks for one day
model DailyPlan {
  id          String      @id @default(uuid())
  date        DateTime                         // the day this plan is for (date only)
  label       String?                          // e.g. "Journée lundi", "Weekend 26-27 Avr"
  isWeekend   Boolean     @default(false)
  teamId      String
  team        Team        @relation(fields: [teamId], references: [id])

  createdById String
  createdBy   User        @relation("PlanCreatedBy", fields: [createdById], references: [id])

  createdAt   DateTime    @default(now())
  updatedAt   DateTime    @updatedAt

  tasks       OperationalTask[]

  @@unique([teamId, date])
  @@index([teamId])
  @@index([date])
}

/// One operational task assigned to one person for a day
model OperationalTask {
  id          String               @id @default(uuid())
  planId      String
  plan        DailyPlan            @relation(fields: [planId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)

  title       String               // short label visible on the board
  description String?              // details / instructions
  taskType    OperationalTaskType  @default(CUSTOM)

  // When during the day
  startTime   DateTime?            // e.g. 07:00 for MEP
  endTime     DateTime?            // e.g. 07:30

  // Who
  assignedToId String
  assignedTo   User               @relation("AssignedOpTasks", fields: [assignedToId], references: [id])

  // What system / chain it concerns
  systemId    String?
  system      System?             @relation(fields: [systemId], references: [id])
  chainLabel  String?             // free text: "Chaîne compta", "Chaîne virements"

  // Status tracking
  status      OperationalTaskStatus @default(TODO)
  note        String?              // operator completion note or blocker reason
  startedAt   DateTime?
  completedAt DateTime?

  priority    TaskPriority         @default(NORMAL)

  createdAt   DateTime             @default(now())
  updatedAt   DateTime             @updatedAt

  @@index([planId])
  @@index([assignedToId])
  @@index([systemId])
  @@index([status])
  @@index([taskType])
}

enum OperationalTaskStatus {
  TODO
  IN_PROGRESS
  DONE
  BLOCKED
}

enum TaskPriority {
  LOW
  NORMAL
  HIGH
  CRITICAL
}
```

